          <caption>
            <p>Moderate-to-Severe Radiation Proctitis on Colonoscopy. This endoscopic view shows the rectal mucosa affected by radiation proctitis, exhibiting multiple telangiectasias, erythema, friable tissue with bleeding spots, and adherent yellowish exudate. Features align with moderate-to-severe grading due to extensive telangiectasia distribution and surface involvement. Tdvorak, <ext-link xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?search=Colonoscopy+of+Radiation+Proctitis&#x00026;title=Special%3AMediaSearch&#x00026;type=image">Public Domain</ext-link>, via Wikimedia Commons</p>
